# LEGACY. Until 2026-08-12 the person's writing lived in memory/; it now lives in
# data/ (see the block further down). This rule stays so that anyone who installed
# before that date, or who puts something here by mistake, is still protected --
# and memory/README.md now says plainly that this folder is not the place.
memory/*
!memory/README.md

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Raw corpus material must never be tracked. The tool unpacks outside the repo by design; this is the
# backstop for a human or a session that puts one here by hand (measured 2026-08-09: 6,228 files).
_unpacked/
*.zip
conversations.json
users.json

# ── YOUR WRITING LIVES HERE, INSIDE THE REPO (layout change, 2026-08-12) ──────
# The tool now clones into the folder you open, so `data` sits inside the
# repository rather than beside it. THIS LINE is what keeps it out of git:
# never tracked, never committed, never uploaded. It replaces the folder
# distance that used to do that job.
#
# ⛔ DO NOT REMOVE IT, and do not let anything add data/ with `git add -f`.
# ⛔ Update with `git pull` — it leaves data/ untouched. NEVER update by
#    deleting this folder and re-cloning; that takes your writing with it.
#    See "Taking an update later" in INSTALL.md.
data/

# ── YOUR KEYS. NEVER COMMITTED. ⚖ the operator's ruling, 2026-08-14 ─────────
# The credential path is a local settings file, chosen deliberately over an OS-native
# keystore for this release (see the plan, F8.8). THESE LINES ARE THE WHOLE PROTECTION,
# so they go in BEFORE the file exists rather than after someone creates one.
#
# ⛔ DO NOT REMOVE, and never `git add -f` one of these. A key in git history is not
#    removed by deleting the file later -- it stays in every clone that ever pulled it,
#    and the only real fix is to rotate the key at the provider.
# ⚠ `git clean -fdX` DELETES ignored files, so this is also the file a cleanup wipes.
#    The tracked template beside it is what makes that recoverable -- keep them in sync.
local.settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Editing debris. A session that is about to rewrite a long file often copies it aside
# first; five of those were sitting untracked in this repo, and a scoped `git add` of a
# directory picked two of them up on 2026-08-11 before the commit was checked. A .bak is
# a safety copy for one session, never a thing to publish — and the guard that stops a
# whole-tree add does not stop a scoped one.
*.bak
*.pre-*.bak
# MISS FOUND 2026-08-24 (verified this session): a timestamp-suffixed backup — e.g.
# `settings.json.bak-20260824-110900` — does not END in `.bak`, so it walks straight past the
# two patterns above. This catches that shape (anything with `.bak-` before a suffix) without
# widening to bare `.bak` mid-name; it does NOT match ordinary tracked files, which have no
# `.bak-` substring at all.
*.bak-*

# ── INTERNAL MIGRATION WORKING NOTES. NEVER SHIPPED. ──────────────────────────
# migration-audit/ is the donor-side project's own scratch: dependency inventories,
# guard-fire test matrices, phase logs — written by and for the person doing the
# port, never for a reader of the product. 08-THIRD-PARTY-INVENTORY.md got tracked
# here by 2026-08-14 (commit ab4cc2a) because it was authored and committed
# directly inside this checkout instead of going through the shipping lane, so
# nothing scrubbed it. It named the operator's own machine paths, a live
# third-party hostname, a locality hint, and a service-by-service map of where
# every credential is stored -- zero value to a student, real value to nobody but
# an attacker. Untracked 2026-08-14; kept on disk, never committed again.
migration-audit/

# the per-install pointer to this brain's notes folder — personal path, NEVER committed
.brain-root

# the per-install personal instruction file — Claude Code auto-loads it alongside
# CLAUDE.md, and it is where an operator's own standing rules belong. Same reasoning
# as .brain-root above: personal content, per-machine, NEVER committed. Ignoring it
# also keeps a tracked copy from colliding with the untracked one every install
# already has. See docs/LOCAL-INSTRUCTIONS.md.
CLAUDE.local.md

# system/organism/generated/ self-declares in its own file header ("DERIVED.
# REGENERATED EVERY RUN. NEVER HAND-EDIT THIS FILE.") as the other machine's
# regenerated output — it was never actually gitignored despite the claim.
# Verified 2026-08-23: no prior rule covered it. Added so the claim matches reality.
system/organism/generated/

# Donor-side spillover that landed inside this checkout instead of the donor's own tree.
# It is the only copy anywhere (absent from every local and remote-tracking ref) and contains
# real personal material. Not deleted or moved, only kept out of version control.
system/parked/2026-08-23-donor-spillover/
